# Environment overrides for deep-research, for CI and one-off changes.
# Most setups need none of this: `drsh setup` picks the model, web search and
# page extraction and stores the keys. Copy to .env in the config directory
# and fill in what you need, or export the matching env var for the session.
# `drsh init` writes the same file for you.
#
# .env is gitignored and must stay that way.

# Get a free OpenRouter key (no card): https://openrouter.ai/keys
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# OPENAI_MODEL=openrouter/free
# Or Claude: your subscription via Claude Code (claude auth login), with this
# key as the fallback.
# DEEP_RESEARCH_PROVIDER=claude
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Web search. Unset means auto: public SearXNG instances from searx.space.
# Set your own instance(s) (comma-separated), or off for LLM search.
# FIRECRAWL_URL adds full page text; without it sources are snippets.
# Setup instructions: docs/services.md.
# SEARXNG_URL=http://localhost:8888
# FIRECRAWL_URL=http://localhost:3002
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=
# Hosted search instead (page text comes with each result; spends credit):
# DEEP_RESEARCH_SEARCH_ENGINE=exa
# EXA_API_KEY=
# DEEP_RESEARCH_SEARCH_ENGINE=tavily
# TAVILY_API_KEY=
